Subject: [PATCH] Anchor the generic scheduler vtable in its implementation

Give GenericSchedulerBase its own out-of-line anchor, following the existing
MachineSchedStrategy convention. Reuse the inherited virtual slot without
changing fields or scheduling operations. The pinned GCC LTO comparison
reports a pure-virtual/scheduleTree mismatch between freshly compiled
MachineScheduler and WindowScheduler despite matching front-end layouts
and native vtable relocations. Keep all compiler warnings enabled.

--- a/thirdparty/llvm-project/llvm/include/llvm/CodeGen/MachineScheduler.h
+++ b/thirdparty/llvm-project/llvm/include/llvm/CodeGen/MachineScheduler.h
@@ -1072,6 +1072,8 @@
 /// scheduling candidates based on TargetSchedModel making it easy to implement
 /// heuristics for either preRA or postRA scheduling.
 class GenericSchedulerBase : public MachineSchedStrategy {
+  LLVM_ABI void anchor() override;
+
 public:
   /// Represent the type of SchedCandidate found within a single queue.
   /// pickNodeBidirectional depends on these listed by decreasing priority.
--- a/thirdparty/llvm-project/llvm/lib/CodeGen/MachineScheduler.cpp
+++ b/thirdparty/llvm-project/llvm/lib/CodeGen/MachineScheduler.cpp
@@ -300,6 +300,8 @@
 // Pin the vtables to this file.
 void MachineSchedStrategy::anchor() {}
 
+void GenericSchedulerBase::anchor() {}
+
 void ScheduleDAGMutation::anchor() {}
 
 //===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
